    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Bali lies between Java and Lombok, a volcanic island ringed by surf beaches. Mount Agung rises over 3,000 metres in the east, and crater lakes like Bratan sit in the cool central highlands.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Most Balinese are Hindu, and every village keeps its own temples and festival calendar. The subak system shares water between rice terraces through canals run by temple councils, and UNESCO listed it in 2012. Ubud is the centre for dance, painting and wood carving. Try babi guling, sate lilit and nasi campur at a warung.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The dry season runs from April to October. On Nyepi, the Balinese New Year in March, the whole island goes silent for a day and the airport closes, so check the date before you book.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
